                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "createdOn": 1774461567,
            "author": {
                "name": "Ender",
                "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
            },
            "kind": "TRIVIAL_REBASE",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 151,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "Is there MCTP VDM command to retrieve number of PCIe functions? Please get the value for number of PCIe functions from inband and see if it is more than on."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaGpuDevice.cpp",
                    "line": 151,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ender",
                        "email": "andhsieh@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "Ender-Hsieh"
                    },
                    "message": "I checked the NSM spec \u2014 there is no MCTP VDM command that returns the number of PCIe functions. The closest is List PCIe Ports (Type 2, Command 0x07), which returns port counts but not function counts.\nVerified from the host side with lspci \u2014 all 8 GPUs expose only function 0:\n$ lspci -nn | grep '3D controller'\n1a:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n1d:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n40:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n43:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n9a:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n9d:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\nbd:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\nc0:00.0 3D controller [0302]: NVIDIA Corporation Device [10de:2bb5] (rev a1)\n\nNo .1, .2, etc. \u2014 each GPU has exactly one PCIe function.\nSince there is no NSM command to retrieve the function count dynamically, and GPU hardware exposes a single function, the current implementation creates one Function0 per GPU device."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 41,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Harshit Aghera",
                        "email": "haghera@nvidia.com",
                        "username": "harshit-aghera"
                    },
                    "message": "use std::format."
                },
                {
                    "file": "src/nvidia-gpu/NvidiaPcieFunction.cpp",
                    "line": 41,
                    "reviewer": {
